## Quick start on Windows

From the repository root:

```powershell
py -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

Launch a compatible Fabric Minecraft instance containing Baritone and the
bridge mod, enter a world, and verify that TCP port `5555` is open:

```powershell
Test-NetConnection localhost -Port 5555
```

Disable pause-on-lost-focus in Minecraft with `F3+P`, then start or resume the
controller:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe spawn_to_dragon.py `
  --host localhost `
  --port 5555 `
  --resume `
  --no-background-systems
```

The Windows wrapper `run_autonomous.bat` performs the same launch and writes
timestamped output under `Logs/`.

## Production progression

The production phase enum lives in
`src/baritone_client/automator/state_manager.py`; handlers live in
`src/baritone_client/automator/phases/`.

| Phase group | Required outcome |
| --- | --- |
| Bridge and bootstrap | Connected, healthy player, durable world checkpoint |
| Initial gathering | Wood, cobblestone, and replaceable stone tools |
| Base construction | Verified house, crafting table, furnace, chest, and food source |
| Food, iron, and enchanting | Renewable food, defensive iron gear, level-30 enchanting |
| Nether and blaze | Persistent portal, fortress location, and blaze rods |
| World unlock | Eyes, stronghold, End portal, explicit Dragon defeat evidence |
| Post-End and megabase | Elytra, shulker boxes, beacon, and terraform plan |

Do not treat a handler returning `True` as proof by itself. Each milestone must
also satisfy its corresponding Suite 1200 acceptance gate and survive a
checkpoint reload.

## Tests: choose the right type

| Test type | Location | Safe for the real autonomous world? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Unit and contract tests | `tests/test_*.py` | Yes; mocked/offline |
| Survival acceptance gates | `tests/functional/survival/` | Read-only, but run when the mutating driver is idle unless concurrent clients are proven safe |
| Legacy functional arenas | `tests/functional/extended_suite_100.py` through `extended_suite_1000.py` | **No**; many use teleport, `/give`, `/setblock`, world clearing, or destructive teardown |
| Persistent farming prototype | `tests/functional/extended_suite_1100.py` | Mutates a live world; run only in an isolated test world |

Run the fast, verified progression regression set:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q `
  tests\test_full_automation.py `
  tests\test_survival_progression.py `
  tests\test_functional_harness.py `
  tests\test_endgame_script.py `
  tests\test_default_handlers.py
```

The full offline collection currently contains 259 tests and includes slow
retry-path coverage. Run `python -m pytest -q` when a longer verification pass
is appropriate.

List functional tests without connecting to Minecraft:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tests\functional\run_tests.py --list
```

Never run the unfiltered functional runner against a world you care about.

## Repository map

```text
bridge/                         Fabric bridge mod; do not modify casually
docs/                           Operator, architecture, and API documentation
artifacts/                      Archived generated reports and captured output
plans/                          Forward-looking designs, not capability claims
scripts/                        Debug, maintenance, adapter, and manual-test tools
src/baritone_client/            Installable Python package
  automator/                    Phase orchestration and checkpoint state
  automator/phases/             Production progression handlers
  common/                       Reusable gameplay capabilities
tests/                          Offline unit and contract tests
tests/functional/               Live Minecraft harness and legacy suites
tests/functional/survival/      Read-only endgame acceptance gates
spawn_to_dragon.py              Primary autonomous runner
run_autonomous.bat              Windows launcher with timestamped logs
```

Generated logs, metrics, checkpoints, debug output, and historical reviews are
not production entry points. See [Repository layout](docs/repository-layout.md)
before moving them because several older documents and scripts still reference
root-level paths.

## Contribution rules

- Read [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) before changing the bridge or automation model.
- Put reusable behavior under `src/baritone_client/`; tests should call
  production behavior rather than maintain a separate implementation.
- Preserve unrelated dirty-worktree changes and the active checkpoint.
- Add an offline test and a Survival acceptance gate for each new capability.
- Do not modify `bridge/` unless the task explicitly targets the Fabric bridge.
